 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Keep a safe distance, and stop at every stop as everyone gets on. It' the only way to be sure nobody has sped through without stopping. Try to speed up a little as you reach the stop, so they don't think you' stopping at every car. Most people appreciate a smooth driver. Stop completely and check both ways every time. It' only a few seconds, and it saves you being nervous for minutes. At first it is, and some people never get over it. But with practice, it becomes second nature, and you realize how rarely anything goes wrong.",
